ion/id #uuid "46340dc9-51f2-5873-b009-41e85ee5bdc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-6670" :question/problem "According to the rational roots theorem, which of the following could be a root of the polynomial $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+17{x}^{2}-10x-9?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial $f(x),$ the constant term is $-9,$ and the leading coefficient is $2.$ So, any rational roots of $f(x)$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of }-9}{\\text{factor of }2}.\n$$\n\nOf the given answer choices, only $-\\frac{9}{2}$ takes the above form since the numerator $(9)$ is a factor of $-9$ and the denominator $(2)$ is a factor of $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083306 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75b47ec-8d5a-545e-b915-daca92320322" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Roots of a Polynomial Using the Rational Roots Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab08216-a85b-52d8-bfb5-9e9512ad46ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333235} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0c3209-4358-57e9-9922-daedefbb9777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333265} {:answer/id #uuid "351fac38-0a31-517e-9482-0406caca8c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333477} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb09eaf-64cc-56f7-960c-192e268f595b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334243} {:answer/id #uuid "f6791d4e-238a-5e79-9